winemac: round the corners of windows without a Mac title bar; window command requests

A Windows program that draws its own title bar gets a borderless Mac window, with square
corners where every Mac window has round ones. Such a window now gets round corners, unless it
is full screen, small (a menu, a tooltip, a splash image) or shaped by its program.
FINEWINE_ROUNDED_WINDOWS=0 turns it off.

Also the window's half of the application menu's commands (previous patch): each asks the
Windows program, as its own title bar buttons would, so they work without a Mac title bar.

